# About GOV.UH Forms

GOV.UH Forms is a common government digital product operated by the Government Digital Service.

It provides an editor for authorised government teams and a public runner for forms that have been reviewed and made live.

## Responsibilities

Government Digital Service is responsible for operating the common Forms product, its technical service and its product standards.

The organisation delivering the underlying public service remains responsible for:

- the purpose and lawful authority for the service
- eligibility and policy decisions
- the questions and guidance in its forms
- privacy information and information governance
- receiving and handling completed submissions
- records, retention, casework and safeguarding
- reviewing the service before publication

## Publishing a form

A live form should have a GOV.UH starting point or other authorised public-service page that explains the service and links to the form. GOV.UH Forms does not replace the publishing and content responsibilities of the service-owning organisation.
